== Problem 1: sort
OK   examples: sort(0110) = 0011, sort(1010) = 0011, sort(101) = 011, sort(111) = 111, sort(ε) = ε
OK   unfolding sort(101): sort(1) = 1, sort(01) = 01, sort(101) = sort(01)•1 = 011
OK   (a) |sort(w)| = |w| for all |w| <= 14
OK   Lemma: sort(y•1) = sort(y)•1 for all |y| <= 14
OK   (b) sort(sort(w)) = sort(w) for all |w| <= 14
OK   closed form: sort(w) = 0^#(0,w) 1^#(1,w) for all |w| <= 14
OK   trap: for w = 1x the string sort(x)•1 is as long as w (the hypothesis does not cover it), |w| <= 12
OK   for w = 1x the lemma is used with y = sort(x), which is shorter than w (|sort(x)| = |w| - 1), on the string sort(x)•1, which is exactly as long as w, |w| <= 12
OK   the first symbol of sort(x)•1 is the attached 1 only when x = ε (otherwise it is the first symbol of sort(x)), |x| <= 12
OK   trap: the look-alike 'sort(y•0) = sort(y)•0' fails at y = 1 (sort(10) = 01, sort(1)•0 = 10)
OK   trap: sort does not distribute over •: sort(1•0) = 01 but sort(1)•sort(0) = 10
